# Database rules (future phase)

Do not add PostgreSQL/pgvector/Prisma/Supabase during the current Next.js AI phase
unless explicitly requested. These rules apply when a real backend database is introduced.

## Principles

- UUID primary keys and `created_at` timestamps by default
- Explicit foreign keys; cascade only where children cannot exist alone
- Timestamps as UTC timestamptz
- Prefer string + CHECK enums over brittle native enum migrations
- Every schema change ships with a reversible migration

## If building Document Intelligence RAG later

Canonical tables may include: `users`, `workspaces`, `documents`, `chunks`,
`conversations`, `messages`, `jobs`, `ai_usage`.

Retrieval must stay workspace-scoped. Chunks used for citations need page/section
metadata — never invent page numbers in the model layer.
